Use `ConfigureLifecycleEvents` in `MauiProgram.cs` to hook platform-native callbacks directly:

```csharp
builder.ConfigureLifecycleEvents(events =>
{
#if ANDROID
    events.AddAndroid(android => android
        .OnPause(activity =>
        {
            // Runs when activity loses focus (notification shade, split-screen)
        })
        .OnStop(activity =>
        {
            // Runs when activity is no longer visible (fully backgrounded)
        }));
#elif IOS || MACCATALYST
    events.AddiOS(ios => ios
        .DidEnterBackground(app =>
        {
            // Runs when app moves to background
        }));
#endif
});
```

**Key points:**

- Android `OnPause` maps to the cross-platform `Deactivated` event; `OnStop` maps to `Stopped`.
- iOS `DidEnterBackground` maps to `Stopped`.
- If you don't need platform-specific APIs, you can use the **cross-platform equivalent** instead — override `OnStopped()` on your `Window` subclass, which fires on both platforms when the app backgrounds.
- Keep handlers fast (<2s) to avoid ANR on Android or watchdog kills on iOS.
- On Android, also handle `OnDestroy` — the back button can skip `OnStop` entirely.
